<h2 id="age-and-claiming">State Pension age, claiming and deferring</h2>

<p>State Pension age is rising from 66 to 67 between 2026 and 2028. The change is happening now. {{ m.c("spa-67") }}</p>

<p>The law provides for a further rise to 68 between 2044 and 2046. {{ m.c("spa-68") }} A third review of State Pension age began in July 2025. {{ m.c("spa-review") }}</p>

<p>The State Pension has to be claimed. {{ m.c("claim-not-automatic") }} A pension that is not claimed is deferred. {{ m.c("deferral-default") }}</p>

<p>Deferring raises the weekly amount later. On the new State Pension the increase is 1% for every {{ m.f("deferral-weeks-new") }} weeks. On the basic State Pension it is 1% for every {{ m.f("deferral-weeks-basic") }} weeks.</p>
{{ m.sourceNote("deferral-weeks-new" | figure) }}

<h2 id="components">Parts of the pension that rise by a different rule</h2>

<p>The triple lock applies to the full rate of the new State Pension and to the basic State Pension. Other parts rise with prices.</p>

